So 0.28*0.28*0.28*0.28*0.28 = 0.00172 chance to fail
five times running, and Janis is quite right to be a
bit miffed in a single instance.

Still, if you engrave Elbereth one time per dungeon
level, that making what, around 70 times, you're
going to see your odds of having that failure five
times in a row happen in a single game at
0.11663906583877328329982268777122, or around one
game in 8 or 9.

The lesson here is that even extremely rare things
_will_ happen in NetHack, you have to be careful not
to generalize one really bad bit of luck into a
threat which you turn into a general rule to avoid
that threat always, when the opposite behavior would
be more in your best interest.

Thus, even if you get badly burned doing it once in
a while, dust engraving Elbereth to save your PC's
life is still a viable strategy all the times your
luck isn't plain stinking horrible.

